{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T12:30:35.563Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"49285cdb3ae2c9d3a7c09636","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T12:30:35.563Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-27T12:30:35.562Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Re-recording branch evidence after adopting the gated sync's item records wholesale (history is a byte-identical prefix-extension of main's; no lines spliced). Reproduction: the retired heading regex measured 1.7s at 800 hostile chars, 13.1s at 1600 (~n^2.8), extrapolating to hours for a 50,000-char line; the retired JSON tokenizer measured linear on every adversarial probe (1MB escaped string 0.03ms, 500k escape pairs 0.2ms, 1MB whitespace 220ms), so alert 1 is a CodeQL false positive on the model, and the tokenizer was still rewritten regex-free so linearity is provable by construction and the alert closes mechanically. Design: headingLines() single-pass per-line parser shared by paragraph() and sectionPath(), byte-identical to the retired regex (curated corpus plus 400 seeded random documents; exact lazy-title and CR-swallow span semantics), and a regex-free JSON scanner with JSON.parse still decoding object keys."}]}],"before_hash":"2f7a9d3ee34101315b68f30be37b874e062e187df918dd42b18a408e5f6c81ae","after_hash":"76415f8e4efcdad3e4d053fe245866b24b40915fb5cf1384ce36aaaff4283ee3","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"2f1db32b06b4fd8704c0d59a98483c01a9baacce7a5655142308715d38d3ef0d"}
